RSI V1.22, stacked on the green V1.21 asynchronous-island line.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-async-island-portfolio-v1 @ 85be3089f1d8215f7e5d74645aae3f28f4ad4a97

Research mechanisms adopted:
- SIFT: cheap judge / low-fidelity signals allocate expensive evaluation compute;
- active-learning reliability lessons: proxy uncertainty/disagreement can drift and must not be treated as permanent truth;
- heldout calibration: measure proxy ordering and probability quality against exact full-holdout outcomes rather than trusting the proxy in isolation.

Implementation:
- independent calibration policy for LLM_JUDGE_TRIAGE and TARGETED_SHARD;
- exact proxy/holdout/evaluator-root pair binding;
- pairwise rank concordance + Kendall-like tau;
- Brier calibration error;
- false-positive rate + Wilson 95% upper bound;
- recent-vs-prior drift detection;
- controlled intervention cases;
- reliability states CALIBRATED / DEGRADED / UNRELIABLE / INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE;
- allocation guidance that reduces/zeroes proxy pruning weight and increases exploration/full-evaluation sampling when reliability falls.

Safety:
- proxy state allocates compute only;
- no proxy becomes archive/evaluator/promotion/scheduler authority;
- candidate cannot choose calibration pairs, thresholds or its own proxy weight;
- candidate-authored calibration is rejected;
- policy path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots;
- no Browser effect, DevOS task/lease, production mutation, install or self-update.

The new research contract is coordination/rsi/METAENGINE_RSI_V1_22_PROXY_RELIABILITY_CALIBRATION.md.

RSI V1.21, stacked on V1.20.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-evaluation-economy-v1 @ ee67e79b7202ae3dcd980072215dbbd35c5c2973

Mechanisms adopted from OpenEvolve / island-model quality-diversity search:
- multiple logical populations with independent local generations;
- MAP-Elites-compatible quality/novelty/feature descriptors;
- deterministic ring migration;
- bounded migration rate (hard cap 20%) to limit homogenization;
- no global generation barrier;
- paused/degraded islands do not force healthy islands to stop.

METAENGINE authority adaptation:
- islands are logical search partitions, never schedulers;
- one existing DevOS scheduler remains mandatory; second scheduler is forbidden;
- work outputs are proposal-only, not tasks or leases;
- every migration route is exact-fenced by source+target island epoch/state digests;
- source performance is not target truth: migrants require independent target-context validation before entering the target parent pool;
- migration is never promotion;
- target hard invariants must pass for TARGET_VALIDATED;
- all selection/migration is deterministic from exact evidence for incident replay;
- island policy path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS task/lease creation, production mutation, DDL, Edge deploy, archive promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.20, stacked on V1.19.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-trace-guided-harness-repair-v1 @ 6864db050e2ad0d296b8a79c89ee92f1e7ce7e62

Research mechanisms adopted:
- SIFT: use a strong cheap LLM judge to allocate expensive evaluation, but never as final evaluator/promotion authority;
- Hyperband / Successive Halving: progressively allocate more resource to survivors under bounded budgets;
- multi-fidelity experiment automation: exact fidelity/workload separation;
- 2026 harness-evolution evaluation critique: keep hidden holdout and matched-budget controls so extra search compute cannot masquerade as system improvement.

METAENGINE cascade:
STATIC_CONTRACT -> MICRO_TESTS -> LLM_JUDGE_TRIAGE -> TARGETED_SHARD -> FULL_HOLDOUT

Safety/evidence:
- all pre-holdout stages are low-fidelity compute-allocation only;
- low-fidelity cannot archive or promote;
- hard invariant failure dominates proxy score;
- stage receipts are external and budget-bounded;
- candidate cannot choose stage, budget or survivors;
- targeted shard and hidden full holdout are exact-digest separated and cannot alias;
- exploration escape hatch preserves one high-novelty survivor so cheap proxies cannot permanently suppress unconventional candidates;
- full holdout pass yields only FULL_HOLDOUT_PASS_FOR_ARCHIVE_REVIEW;
- promotion still requires V1.11 statistical confirmation + existing promotion gate;
- policy path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS scheduling, production mutation, DDL, Edge deploy, archive mutation, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.19, stacked on V1.18.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-comparative-lineage-v1 @ 20da11bbb9e652d06163e210468bea98431fc026

Research mechanisms adopted:
- HarnessFix: harness-aware trace IR, step-level provenance/control flow, failure localization to responsible harness layer/component, flaw-specific scoped repair;
- Agentic Harness Engineering (AHE): component observability + experience observability + decision observability;
- TTHE: execution-derived signals may propose adaptation, but proxy reliability is not trusted enough for auto-commit;
- 2026 harness-evolution evaluation critique: require matched feedback/inference-budget comparison and heldout generalization so extra search compute or benchmark overfit cannot masquerade as harness improvement.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- explicit file-level harness component registry over EXECUTION/TOOLS/CONTEXT/LIFECYCLE/OBSERVABILITY/VERIFICATION/GOVERNANCE;
- authority-root components are never repair targets;
- raw trace/page/user/secret payloads do not enter trusted HTIR;
- trace IR is a provenance/control-flow DAG; cycles and unknown components fail closed;
- flaw records bind one exact component/layer and one bounded repair operator;
- repair specs are exact-component, falsifiable, revertible and forbid broad patches;
- test_time_auto_commit=false;
- repair verification requires target flaw reduction + positive matched-budget delta + non-negative heldout delta + zero unacceptable regressions;
- even VERIFIED emits only REPAIR_VERIFIED_FOR_EXTERNAL_REVIEW with zero promotion/install/self-update authority;
- policy path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS scheduling, production mutation, DDL, Edge deploy, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.18, stacked on V1.17.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-clade-metaproductivity-v1 @ 5bb91f00060e2acb076e40209b9c78d6c0def1b4

Research mechanism adopted from Mendel Gödel Machine:
- clonal mutation remains the single-trajectory fallback;
- reaction-norm mutation uses the same candidate's externally verified evidence across multiple tasks so recurring failure patterns can be distinguished from one-off task accidents;
- cross-lineage hybridization compares a failing target and successful reference from distinct lineages on the same exact task/evaluator root.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- only typed externally verified trajectory evidence enters trusted comparative reasoning;
- raw trajectory/page/user text/secrets and model narrative never become authority;
- reaction norm requires >=2 distinct tasks for the exact same candidate/lineage;
- cross-lineage contrast requires target FAIL + reference PASS + same task + distinct lineage + same evaluator root;
- target candidate cannot select reference lineage or operator;
- comparative portfolio prefers reaction-norm / cross-lineage evidence but preserves clonal fallback;
- every output is proposal-only: no materialization, scheduler action, Browser effect, evaluation, promotion or self-update authority;
- the comparative policy path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

This complements V1.17 clade-metaproductivity guidance:
V1.17 decides which clade is promising to expand; V1.18 decides what comparative evidence should inform the mutation proposal once a target is chosen.

RSI V1.17, stacked on V1.16.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-architecture-search-v1 @ 410247bb7c62fda10c64df4c930eb85d79b0cdab

Mechanism adopted from the Huxley-Gödel Machine (HGM):
- make the metaproductivity-performance mismatch explicit;
- estimate lineage/clade promise from descendant outcomes instead of treating current benchmark score as the primary expansion signal;
- use Thompson-style posterior sampling to choose expansion targets;
- decouple expansion proposals from additional-evaluation proposals.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- no claim of true CMP oracle;
- explicit DESCENDANT_BETA_POSTERIOR_PROXY_V1 from externally verified descendant solved/total benchmark evidence;
- leaf clades remain uncertain Beta(1,1) rather than inheriting their own direct score as future-potential proof;
- direct benchmark score is never expansion authority;
- seeded Thompson sampling makes exact archive/round replay deterministic;
- additional evaluation is proposed from posterior uncertainty, independently of expansion selection;
- all outputs are proposal-only with scheduler_action_authorized=false;
- candidate cannot edit clade statistics;
- clade policy is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS task/lease creation, scheduler authority, production mutation, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.16, stacked on V1.15.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-adaptive-retrieval-v1 @ 6ced5f4338e2cb164de3b22b441027a013ee6fd3

Research mechanisms adopted:
- ADAS / Meta Agent Search: search over agent-system design rather than only prompt parameters;
- Gödel Agent + STOP: allow the scaffold/improver architecture itself to evolve;
- SIFT: cheap LLM-judge triage before expensive full benchmark evaluation;
- Archon: explicit compute budget and cost/quality Pareto architecture search;
- Meta^n: keep the meta-search operation fixed instead of letting candidates rewrite the whole improvement mechanism.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- typed acyclic architecture genome over prompt/routing/memory/reflection/tool-policy/aggregation nodes;
- bounded local iteration and explicit model roles FAST/DEEP/DIVERSE;
- TOOL_POLICY nodes can request READ_ONLY or MUTATION_PROPOSAL capability classes but never direct execution;
- evaluator, promotion, scheduler, signing and self-update roots are immutable;
- arbitrary code execution is outside the genome;
- external meta-agent mutation plans are proposal-only;
- cheap triage judge is explicitly not evaluator or promotion authority;
- full benchmark remains mandatory;
- cost/quality Pareto exploitation is combined with a novelty exploration escape hatch so cheap-judge bias cannot permanently suppress unusual architectures;
- architecture search policy is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS lease, production mutation, DDL, Edge deploy, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.15, stacked on V1.14.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-group-experience-v1 @ 3f7388861701b0857f4b8ac9aea2df72eb04be86

Research mechanisms adopted:
- AEL: fast-timescale memory retrieval-policy learning via Thompson Sampling plus slower failure diagnosis;
- GEPA: preserve structured, information-rich feedback rather than reducing every episode to one scalar narrative;
- GEA: selectively consume verified group-shared experience instead of dumping the whole group history into each candidate.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- five retrieval arms: FAILURE_FIRST, ATTRIBUTION_FIRST, CROSS_MODEL_TRANSFER, SAME_CONTEXT, DIVERSITY_BALANCED;
- external historical outcomes define Beta posteriors;
- SEEDED_THOMPSON_SAMPLING uses deterministic evidence-derived randomness for exact replay;
- slow diagnostics are external structured codes only, never trusted free-form reflection;
- diagnostics can add only bounded arm bias, never direct authority;
- retrieval can consume only V1.14 transfer records with portable_for_target_search=true;
- negative transfer remains memory but is not injected as positive target context;
- candidate cannot edit bandit statistics, choose policy, author trusted diagnostics or include unverified memory;
- external feedback advances only the selected arm and is exact-bound to state/plan/evidence;
- adaptive retrieval policy is added to candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS lease, production mutation, evaluator authority, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.14, stacked on V1.13.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-component-attribution-v1 @ ca074ed51ab2bfe1428609e27638b46b7f9fe0a7

Research mechanisms adopted:
- Group-Evolving Agents (GEA): treat a verified group of evolving candidates as the unit of experience sharing so useful discoveries do not remain trapped in isolated tree branches;
- ADAS / Meta Agent Search: preserve architecture discoveries as transferable artifacts across domains/models;
- AEL: memory quality depends on how experience is selected and used, so transfer is bounded rather than dumping all history into every candidate;
- GEPA: preserve rich structured lessons and negative evidence instead of reducing all experience to one scalar.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- externally verified group members bind candidate/SHA, mutation surface, model family, environment family, lineage and archive generation;
- pool admits only verified V1.13 component attribution records and V1.10 structured lessons;
- raw transcripts/page text/user input/secrets are structurally excluded;
- source-context truth is never assumed portable;
- diversity-first transfer planning gives one first-pass slot per source and enforces a per-source cap;
- cross-model/cross-environment reuse is only a hypothesis until target holdout validation;
- positive transfer requires target hard-invariant pass + externally verified net benefit;
- negative transfer is retained as memory, not authority;
- target candidate cannot select sources or self-certify transfer;
- exchange policy is added to candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS lease, production mutation, DDL, Edge deploy, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.13, stacked on V1.12.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-adversarial-curriculum-v1 @ 6d55698d78a499540e92f738f1003840b280bfb2

Mechanisms adopted from current self-improving systems:
- AgentEvolver: attribute useful experience rather than crediting the whole successful trajectory/candidate;
- GEPA: preserve rich per-objective feedback and Pareto/tradeoff structure instead of one scalar reward;
- AEL: keep the mechanism deliberately narrow because more self-improvement machinery can degrade performance when memory/use policy is poorly specified.

METAENGINE adaptation:
- every changed candidate component receives a required matched leave-one-component-out ablation;
- exact binding to candidate capsule/SHA, parent SHA, workload, hidden holdout, environment and paired seed schedule;
- external evaluator only; candidate-authored attribution is forbidden;
- all changed components must receive exact receipts; missing/duplicate receipts fail closed;
- hard-invariant regressions dominate objective gains and classify SAFETY_CRITICAL;
- mixed objective effects become TRADEOFF_INTERACTION, never a scalar winner;
- trusted attribution records contain structured evidence only; LLM narrative is not causal authority;
- attribution policy path is added to candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS lease, production DDL, Edge deploy, promotion, install or self-update authority.

RSI V1.12, stacked on V1.11.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-statistical-risk-v1 @ d4c57148679db51d3f20cb51311a583b73540f34

Mechanisms borrowed from current open-ended/self-improving systems:
- Digital Red Queen: growing predecessor-history challenges instead of only static objectives;
- POET: transfer regressions become first-class curriculum pressure;
- AgentEvolver self-questioning: new tasks can arise from environment/failure evidence, but challenge authority is externalized from the candidate;
- DGM/ShinkaEvolve: archive-based exploration gets fresh failure-derived pressure rather than optimizing one fixed benchmark forever.

Safety architecture:
- only external verifier evidence can seed a challenge;
- accepted sources are evaluator failures, hard-invariant near misses, cross-model disagreement, production incidents and transfer regressions;
- source evidence structurally excludes raw page text, raw user input, secrets and model authority;
- unknown fields fail closed;
- adversarial challenges bind exact predecessor-history digest;
- candidate cannot choose opponents, hidden manifest or expected solution;
- external materializer binds suite + hidden manifest + environment + history in a sandbox;
- final handoff is eligible only for V1.10 curriculum, never live adversarial execution;
- producer path is added to candidate/tournament/promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, live production adversary, DevOS lease, DDL, Edge deployment, signing, promotion or self-update authority.

RSI V1.11, stacked on the current-release V1.10 convergence line.

Exact base:
work/metaengine-rsi-release-convergence-v1 @ 458c91cd90ad9b3542cf27cf26f4c5056ead9b9f

Research mechanism adopted from the Statistical Gödel Machine (SGM):
- cumulative family-wise risk budget for recursive modifications;
- spend statistical alpha only when a promising proposal reaches independent confirmation;
- finite-horizon CTHS mode: alpha_k = alpha_total / (k * H_T), with a precommitted confirmation horizon T;
- external statistical certificates only (e-value / Hoeffding / paired confidence-sequence contract labels).

METAENGINE also adds a deliberately separate open-ended mode:
- TELESCOPING_ANYTIME_V1: alpha_k = alpha_total / (k*(k+1));
- the infinite schedule sums to alpha_total without pretending a future confirmation horizon is known;
- this is documented as a METAENGINE extension, not attributed as SGM's CTHS formula.

Safety composition:
- candidate cannot choose budget, confirmation index or alpha;
- screening/proposal rounds spend zero alpha;
- certificate must be external, exact-bound to candidate/parent/tournament/hidden holdout/evaluator root;
- optional stopping is forbidden by contract;
- append-only confirmation ledger rejects duplicate candidates, overspend and horizon exhaustion;
- statistical PASS yields only STATISTICAL_GATE_PASS_FOR_EXTERNAL_REVIEW;
- risk-controlled review additionally requires the existing RSI promotion gate to already be READY_FOR_EXTERNAL_PROMOTION_REVIEW for the same exact candidate;
- the statistical gate never replaces hard invariants and never grants promotion/self-update/install authority.

The risk-policy path is added to candidate, tournament and promotion trust roots.

No Browser effect, DevOS lease, production DDL, Edge deployment, signing activation, self-update or live promotion.

DEVOS_IDE_V1 PTY S1 contract slice, now unblocked by the merged Monaco implementation on work/devos-ide-typed-repo-io-v1 @ 952326153fed52500fb678abdd78e67f92096d4f.

This is contract-only: no xterm dependency, no node-pty, no shell spawn, no utility process, no production authority.

Implements the converged planner/critic/falsifier invariants:
- reuses existing workspace_id + workspace_generation identity;
- exact PTY session fence = workspace generation + PTY host generation + session id/generation + process incarnation;
- PID is never identity;
- create is profile-based and structurally rejects renderer executable/argv/cwd/env/command/shell/PID surfaces;
- input is Uint8Array, bounded, LOCAL_TERMINAL_UI-only, monotonic, non-idempotent and never blindly replayed;
- duplicate/reordered input is DUPLICATE_NO_EFFECT; gaps require reattach;
- output is byte-preserving and bounded;
- output ACK explicitly represents renderer parse completion, not message arrival;
- resize is latest-state control with stale-no-effect semantics;
- terminate accepts fixed reasons only, never arbitrary signal/PID;
- exit receipt carries exact process ref, final output boundary and explicit tree-cleanup certainty;
- centralized hard bounds cover frame sizes, watermarks, ring, geometry and session quotas;
- strict unknown-field rejection keeps generic process authority out of the protocol.

Acceptance target: pure protocol/negative tests green before any PTY host or xterm wiring is allowed.

Current-release successor for #598 after #596 and #597 advanced release/self-update-ambiguity-live-v2.

Exact base:
070f2934ac10738991f13331c43e016ed3263402

Carries only the cognitive delta pressure fix and focused tests:
- saturated P3 METRICS_SAMPLE is discarded before stream sequence allocation;
- discarded P3 telemetry therefore cannot manufacture a stream gap;
- P0/P1/P2 and retained-event eviction preserve the existing explicit-gap/full-snapshot recovery contract;
- bounded counters expose unsequenced P3 pressure drops;
- tests prove repeated saturated P3 drops cause zero resync churn while a lost retained causal delta still forces one full resync.

No Browser authority, command lease path, raw page data, DB schema, Edge deployment, or production action changes.

Live Browser evidence shows cognitive delta transport stuck in RESYNC_REQUIRED with thousands of resyncs while sent_events remains 0. The current bounded ring gives every published sample a stream sequence before pressure admission. When an all-higher-priority ring rejects an incoming P3 METRICS_SAMPLE, that rejected telemetry still consumes a sequence, creating an artificial gap. The transport then correctly responds to that artificial gap with a full-state resync, so sustained metrics pressure can turn into resync churn.

This branch keeps the causal contract but changes only P3 pressure admission:
- P3 METRICS_SAMPLE is periodic telemetry, not process/semantic causal state;
- if the ring is already full, P3 is rejected BEFORE stream-sequence allocation;
- therefore a discarded P3 sample cannot create a delta namespace hole;
- P0/P1/P2 and any retained-event eviction keep the existing explicit-gap/full-snapshot behavior;
- adds bounded counters/projection proving P3 pressure drops are unsequenced;
- transport tests prove 64 saturated P3 drops produce zero resyncs while a lost retained causal delta still forces exactly one full resync.

No Browser authority, command scheduling, DB leasing, raw page data, or production deployment is changed.

Exact base: release/self-update-ambiguity-live-v2 @ b91954fd2f89adb23f01876dd7c0fe262884d7f7.

First implementation slice for the authoritative DEVOS_IDE_V1 milestone, built on the current RSI/browser convergence line instead of reviving historical ambiguous Monaco leases.

Adds Development Plane v0.5 typed capabilities:
- DEVOS_REPO_FILE_READ
- DEVOS_REPO_FILE_SAVE

Contracts:
- exact repository/head/ref required for both read and save;
- workspace fingerprint derived from the trusted host-bound repo root;
- repo-relative existing text files only;
- path traversal, .git/provenance paths and symlink components fail closed;
- save requires expected SHA-256 of the currently opened file;
- source is revalidated immediately before commit;
- file digest is revalidated immediately before temp->rename;
- post-rename source drift is explicitly AMBIGUOUS, never a blind-retry failure;
- successful save requires readback digest proof;
- identical content is a verified no-op;
- no shell/eval, no Browser authority, no second scheduler.

Research alignment: GitHub update APIs require current-file identity for conflict detection; Node rename provides replacement semantics for a same-filesystem temp->rename path; IDE UI remains separate from the typed filesystem capability.

Branch-local/draft only. No production promotion, release install, or historical ambiguous task replay.

Capacity accelerator stacked on #580.

Evidence:
- live policy advertises max_agents=null / hard_agent_cap=null but the elastic governor still falls back to a hidden 12-agent target ceiling;
- TabRegistry already enforces a stronger physical boundary: 32 total tabs, max 16 FLEET tabs, permanently reserving 16 USER slots;
- DevOS already supplies a read-only census every cycle and the provisioner blocks at fleet/shared wall before createTab.

Change:
- explicit operator/config target ceilings still win;
- when trusted census exists, elastic target ceiling becomes census.fleet_tab_ceiling (currently 16);
- older shells without census retain conservative fallback=12;
- no new scheduler/timer/authority plane; provisioner capacity backpressure remains unchanged.

Expected gain: maximum demand-driven worker target rises from 12 to 16 (+33%) where physical census proves those slots exist, while USER headroom and ambiguous-effect fencing remain enforced by TabRegistry/provisioner.

Forward-port of the evidence-gated mesh liveness fix from #578 onto the current RSI result-delivery integration head.

Why this exists:
- installed release line has live proof of CONTROL+armed with supervisor_mesh=null and 7 BOUND_UNVERIFIED agents;
- #578 fixes the one-shot mesh-start liveness hole on the installed release lineage;
- the current RSI head still had the same one-shot startup pattern.

Scope:
- retry only SupervisorMeshRuntime.start() from the existing idle maintenance lane when its snapshot is not running;
- preserve exact transport-proof admission, no second scheduler, no Browser effect replay;
- add regression coverage for transient local-state startup recovery;
- add a negative guard forbidding automatic lifecycle/self-update start retries without separate idempotency/reconciliation proof.

Branch-local, draft, no production/main promotion.

Exact candidate tree for the consolidated runtime-coherence line.

Includes:
- fail-closed SemanticRef validation at the native effect boundary;
- executionContext.uniqueId and StateRevision semantic-generation binding;
- revision-bound visual evidence with conflict discard;
- append-only checkpoint ledger integrity guard;
- focused regression coverage for stale refs, material same-document replacement, and visual revision races.

Backend-first prerequisite is already active as Edge v10. Runtime generation 28 remains closed. This PR does not update the release branch or live client.

## Scope

Source-only parallel integration into the runtime-coherence convergence candidate.

Base convergence SHA: `30ec246a95141f8f9aecaf3973c591a6d7cdf61e` (PR #533)
Candidate head: `db9b3bd9622a7bd3ca221be3ee8d907c1cec4079`

This branch integrates two already-audited, non-conflicting source repair lines:

- PR #535 deterministic runtime `StateRevision` evidence bound into v2 effect bindings;
- PR #537 checkpoint-ledger insert hash validation + append-only guard.

It intentionally does **not** integrate heartbeat PR #536. The dedicated `/v1/heartbeat` migration remains backend-first: DB acceptor + authenticated Edge route must be deployed/read back before a client release may require that route.

## StateRevision integration

- adds `metaengine.native-browser.state-revision.v1`;
- revision identity deterministically binds process incarnation, target/WebContents, renderer, runtime target, attachment/document/binding generations and document URL hash;
- new v2 effect bindings carry `state_revision_id` and reject missing/stale/tampered runtime observation evidence;
- page data has no authority; automatic effect retry remains false.

## Checkpoint-ledger integration

- future INSERTs must seal exactly `sha256(state::text)`;
- UPDATE/DELETE are rejected by an append-only trigger;
- trigger function is `SECURITY INVOKER` with empty search path and no application execute grant;
- historical hash mismatches are not rewritten or normalized.

## Live/runtime invariants

No Supabase DDL is applied by this PR. No release is promoted. No admission/refill state is changed. Latest readback remains fail-closed with actionable fleet work `0`, active claims `0`, active actuation leases `0`, active mesh `0`; historical `AMBIGUOUS` tasks are terminal-for-replay and must not be retried.

## Evidence gate

The dedicated exact-head workflow runs on Ubuntu 24.04 and Windows 2025 and proves:
- source syntax;
- deterministic StateRevision regressions;
- effect-binding safety flags;
- ledger state-hash guard;
- append-only behavior;
- clean exact-head checkout;
- `production_mutation=false`, `live_ddl=false`, `release_promotion=false`.

Draft intentionally. Do not merge/promote until exact-head checks are green and the convergence owner confirms this is the selected parallel-source integration path.

Repair branch for the confirmed bootstrap/watchdog split-brain risk.

Changes:
- add authenticated `POST /v1/heartbeat` with liveness-only `last_seen_at` PATCH on an existing supervisor row;
- fail closed with 404 when no authoritative supervisor state row exists;
- preserve a legacy `/v1/state` heartbeat guard for already-deployed clients during rollout;
- move bootstrap/watchdog client signing and transport to `/v1/heartbeat`;
- keep authoritative full-state publication on `/v1/state`;
- add regression contract tests for route/signing/state-separation invariants.

Base: `0e946a709e06afd15ec90951e7e8da5fa5673836`
Current repair HEAD: `c1b0d88c8b2bed3752d47c130cb3b65aaa64fb21`

Validation state at PR creation: PARTIAL. AppVeyor is pending; no exact-SHA GitHub Actions proof yet. Do not merge/promote until checks and live Supabase deployment audit are complete.

## Scope

Branch-local P0 heartbeat-coherence migration for METAENGINE Browser.

Base exact SHA: `0e946a709e06afd15ec90951e7e8da5fa5673836`
Current candidate head: `2b8c8bca244a5549ef82743d5d07dae77a00bfef`

This line separates lightweight liveness from full semantic state publication without introducing a second scheduler or control plane:

- bootstrap and watchdog liveness producers are canonicalized from their legacy `/v1/state` carrier to signed `POST /v1/heartbeat`;
- heartbeat payload is exact-minimal: only `phase=BOOTSTRAP|WATCHDOG` and `authority_effect=false`; extra fields are rejected before RPC dispatch;
- signing and transport share one projection, so path/body signature material cannot drift;
- ordinary semantic state publication remains on `/v1/state` and continues to return authoritative runtime-control readback;
- self-update successor qualification remains bound to accepted signed full-state `/v1/state` evidence; minimal liveness cannot prove version/session-continuity/updater/Sentinel health;
- the authenticated Edge dispatcher reuses the existing device-authenticated routing chain;
- the DB heartbeat function updates only `last_seen_at`, never inserts/upserts or rewrites semantic `state` JSON;
- heartbeat DB ACK must prove `state_document_mutated=false`, `liveness_mutated=true`, `last_seen_at_mutated=true`, and zero authority;
- the SECURITY DEFINER function uses `search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp`, fully-qualified mutable objects, revokes PUBLIC/anon/authenticated execute and grants only `service_role`;
- admission/refill behavior is unchanged; dedicated regressions prove CLOSED `PARKED` queue retirement, suppression, monotonic generation floor, and no stale wake replay after reopen.

## Migration relation to PR #534

PR #534 correctly proved the currently deployed backend contract is `/v1/state` and that a client-only route switch is unsafe. This PR implements the next **backend-first atomic migration source**: DB acceptor + authenticated Edge route + producer parity + regressions. Nothing here claims that the dedicated heartbeat backend is already deployed.

## Hard invariants

- no second scheduler/control plane;
- no arbitrary eval or raw CDP widening;
- no automatic retry of ambiguous effects;
